{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/997407-npc-sunny-and-the-kid","id":997407,"title":"[NPC] Sunny and the Kid","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T15:36:47-07:00","id":997407,"title":"[NPC] Sunny and the Kid","content":"<i>&quot;Howdy!</i><br /> <i>I'm</i> <span style=\"color:#FFD700\">SUNNY</span>.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFD700\">SUNNY</span> <i>the</i> <span style=\"color:#FFD700\">SUNFLOWER</span><i>!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Sunny is a big friendly sunflower in a cramped little clay pot carried around by a quiet dead-eyed kid. Sunny is also a plant <i><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/997352-kryptae-and-se-irim\">kryptae</a> </i>that managed to put down roots in the fallen body of a Centimanus and extract enough Vitriol and memories from its innards to fan its dim spark of awareness into something deep, complex, and utterly malevolent. It understands its situation well enough to know that it has intelligence, but no physical ability to act on the world or even speak. It knows it has reason, but no capacity for empathy. It has a future, but no hope. It could simply die if it ran out of Pyros, but it fears death and the end of awareness more than it fears its own continued misery.<br /> <br /> What it <i>does </i>have is the capacity to manipulate. Flux has granted it the power to put down roots in the dreams of Prometheans, and perhaps other supernatural beings as well. And in dreams and visions, it can communicate. It plays the helpful advisor, passing on insights and warnings or just being a sympathetic ear in a lonely and hostile world. And inevitably, it tries to see what it can make its new playmate do. It treats the world something like a videogame, with characters it can use to do helpful or horrifying things until it gets bored of them and moves on, with no consequences to the actual player.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Sunny the Sunflower</b></u><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 1<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 4, Persuasion 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Residual Memory (Occult, Persuasion, Subterfuge) 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 0<br /> <b>Health:</b> 2<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Catharsis (as the Contamination Distillation, using Occult instead of Empathy), Consume Vitriol (using Occult), Dream Seeing [1]*, Dream Shaping [1]*, Sense Vitriol, Track Pyros, Unholy Repast [5]<br /> <br /> (*from <b>Mortal Remains</b> pages 148-49)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Kid is an inexperienced and apparently mute Centimanus with a child's body whom Sunny has manipulated, gaslighted and browbeaten into carrying its flowerpot around and introducing it to new Prometheans. This way it can be replanted as needed, set down near someone's sleeping body, or fed Pyros by soaking its soil in Promethean blood. Sunny is utterly dependent on the Kid, but it has no empathy or affection for them, only contempt. It tends to express this by entering the Kid's dreams and reminding them how much suffering they have enabled by carting Sunny around, and how hopeless their situation is. Maybe a sympathetic throng could pull them away from Sunny's influence and back onto the Pilgrimage after crossing paths. Or maybe the Kid is much, much worse than Sunny could ever be.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Kid</b></u><br /> <b>Lineage:</b> Extempore<br /> <b>Refinement:</b> Centimani<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Investigation 2, Medicine 2, Occult (Flux) 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival 2, Weaponry (Knife) 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Subterfuge (Harmless) 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Defensive Combat (Weaponry) 1, Fighting Finesse (Weaponry) 2, Small-Framed 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Pilgrimage:</b> 1<br /> <b>Elpis:</b> Determination<br /> <b>Torment: </b>Merciless<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3/6 with weapon<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 6<br /> <b>Azoth:</b> 2<br /> <b>Pyros/per Turn:</b> 11/2<br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> But it Refused (see below)<br /> <b>Transmutations:</b> Flux - Blight, Solvent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-02-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"ra