t <i>does </i>have is the capacity to manipulate. Flux has granted it the power to put down roots in the dreams of Prometheans, and perhaps other supernatural beings as well. And in dreams and visions, it can communicate. It plays the helpful advisor, passing on insights and warnings or just being a sympathetic ear in a lonely and hostile world. And inevitably, it tries to see what it can make its new playmate do. It treats the world something like a videogame, with characters it can use to do helpful or horrifying things until it gets bored of them and moves on, with no consequences to the actual player.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Sunny the Sunflower</b></u><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 1<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 5<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Occult 4, Persuasion 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits: </b>Residual Memory (Occult, Persuasion, Subterfuge) 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Size:</b> 1<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 0<br /> <b>Health:</b> 2<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Catharsis (as the Contamination Distillation, using Occult instead of Empathy), Consume Vitriol (using Occult), Dream Seeing [1]*, Dream Shaping [1]*, Sense Vitriol, Track Pyros, Unholy Repast [5]<br /> <br /> (*from <b>Mortal Remains</b> pages 148-49)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;...&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Kid is an inexperienced and apparently mute Centimanus with a child's body whom Sunny has manipulated, gaslighted and browbeaten into carrying its flowerpot around and introducing it to new Prometheans. This way it can be replanted as needed, set down near someone's sleeping body, or fed Pyros by soaking its soil in Promethean blood. Sunny is utterly dependent on the Kid, but it has no empathy or affection for them, only contempt. It tends to express this by entering the Kid's dreams and reminding them how much suffering they have enabled by carting Sunny around, and how hopeless their situation is. Maybe a sympathetic throng could pull them away from Sunny's influence and back onto the Pilgrimage after crossing paths. Or maybe the Kid is much, much worse than Sunny could ever be.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Kid</b></u><br /> <b>Lineage:</b> Extempore<br /> <b>Refinement:</b> Centimani<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Investigation 2, Medicine 2, Occult (Flux) 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival 2, Weaponry (Knife) 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Subterfuge (Harmless) 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Defensive Combat (Weaponry) 1, Fighting Finesse (Weaponry) 2, Small-Framed 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Pilgrimage:</b> 1<br /> <b>Elpis:</b> Determination<br /> <b>Torment: </b>Merciless<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3/6 with weapon<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 6<br /> <b>Azoth:</b> 2<br /> <b>Pyros/per Turn:</b> 11/2<br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> But it Refused (see below)<br /> <b>Transmutations:</b> Flux - Blight, Solvent</div> </div> </div> </div>Stolen! So, so so stolen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T07:36:19-08:00","id":1055228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/997407-npc-sunny-and-the-kid?p=997509#post997509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>And you know what the best part of all this is?<br /> You'll come back.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Again.</span></b><br /> And <span style=\"color:#FFD700\"><b>again.</b></span><br /> And <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><u><b>again!</b></u></span><br /> <br /> Because you want a &amp;quot;<b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">happy ending</span>.</b>&amp;quot;<br /> Because you &amp;quot;<b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">believe you can be human</span>.</b>&amp;quot;<br /> Because you &amp;quot;<b><span style=\"color:#FFD700\">never give up</span>.</b>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Isn't that delicious?<br /> Your <b>&amp;quot;<span style=\"color:#FFD700\">Bestowment</span>...&amp;quot;</b><br /> The power that let you get this far...<br /> It's gonna be your downfall!</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Kid's Bestowment: But it Refused</b><br /> The Kid doesn't die. Ever. If there's even a shred of hope remaining, they can come back swinging. But this isn't an enlightening journey to the Underworld like the Revivification Bestowment. Their body simply refuses to die, drawing on the power of Flux to reinvigorate itself.<br /> <br /> When the Kid marks their last Health box with aggravated damage, it immediately triggers a Praxidikae Firestorm centered on them. At the conclusion of the Firestorm, they may spend a Willpower <i>dot </i>to immediately revivify, regain Health equal to their Azoth, and gain two dots in a Dread Power of the Storyteller's choosing. This triggers a Wasteland as normal for reviving.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Unexpected rules consequence: the nature of Lilithian Firestorms and Sunny's Health means it won't survive the Kid's Bestowment if it's nearby, which it almost definitely would be. If you want to give the poor little flower a slim chance of hanging on, you might grant it Stamina 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>ALSO stolen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}